      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "high",
      "judgment": false,
      "rule": "No dressed quoin of any kind. In a mass-wall cottage the corner is simply the wall material itself, rounded rather than arrised — cob in particular will not hold a sharp corner at all (diagnostic_tells: 'wall corners visibly curved because cob will not hold a sharp arris'). Contrast cotswold-vernacular, whose corners take a dressed ashlar quoin.",
