            4,
            8
          ],
          "unit": "percent",
          "kind": "measured",
          "note": "Against 15-20 percent in a Georgian house of the same date; the window tax (1696-1851) is part of the reason."
        }
      },
      "rule": "Openings are small — roughly 2'0\"-3'3\" wide by 2'3\"-3'11\" high — and few: glazed area runs only 4-8 percent of floor area, well under a Georgian house's 15-20 percent of the same date.",
      "sources": [
